  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734228",
      "title": "Adding User Logout",
      "sourceHash": "5cb7135e84a256d3fbf2f341bf1fb8084b748a75c660684b443f6ed7c33f7154",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.66,
          "en": "Now getting that token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.66,
          "end": 6.57,
          "en": "storing it and attaching it to outgoing requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.57,
          "end": 8.4,
          "en": "is an important part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.4,
          "end": 9.96,
          "en": "But we can now also go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.96,
          "end": 12.42,
          "en": "to our fronted application itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.42,
          "end": 15.99,
          "en": "We might want to update the user interface based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.99,
          "end": 18.6,
          "en": "on the current authentication status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.6,
          "end": 22.35,
          "en": "If we have a token, for example, we might not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.35,
          "end": 25.83,
          "en": "want to show this authentication navigation item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.83,
          "end": 27.48,
          "en": "because it makes no sense to show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 29.613,
          "en": "that if we are locked in already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.69,
          "end": 33.48,
          "en": "On the other hand, it makes no sense to show the edit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.48,
          "end": 36.03,
          "en": "and delete buttons or this new event button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.03,
          "end": 39.66,
          "en": "if we are not locked in, because allowing users to go there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.66,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "if we're not locked in makes also no sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "So updating the UI based on the existence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 48.33,
          "en": "of a token makes a lot of sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.33,
          "end": 49.53,
          "en": "However, that also means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 52.59,
          "en": "that we need a way of getting rid of a token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.59,
          "end": 55.23,
          "en": "And at the moment, we would have to do that manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.23,
          "end": 56.94,
          "en": "through the dev tools, which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.94,
          "end": 59.943,
          "en": "of course not the solution we wanna offer to our users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.02,
          "end": 64.53,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna add a log out route, and that means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.53,
          "end": 69.03,
          "en": "that in MainNavigation.js in our navigation component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.03,
          "end": 74.03,
          "en": "we wanna add a new list item to our navigation bar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.19,
          "end": 78.60300000000001,
          "en": "that in the end shows a log out button like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.19,
          "end": 84.18,
          "en": "Now this button should then trigger an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.18,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "or whatever that deletes the token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 89.7,
          "en": "And there are different ways of handling this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.7,
          "end": 92.03999999999999,
          "en": "We could simply add a on click listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.03999999999999,
          "end": 93.87,
          "en": "and trigger a function that reaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.87,
          "end": 96.87,
          "en": "out to local storage and deletes the token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.87,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "But here I'll use the more official React Routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 104.52000000000001,
          "en": "Embracing approach, and I'll add a new route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.52000000000001,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "I'll add a new file in my pages folder called Logout.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 111.57,
          "en": "And the special thing about this file is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.57,
          "end": 114.33,
          "en": "that it actually won't contain any component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.33,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "because there is no log out page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 120.6,
          "en": "Instead, I'll just export a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.6,
          "end": 124.29,
          "en": "and action to be precise, which will clear my local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.29,
          "end": 125.913,
          "en": "which will get rid of the token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.81,
          "end": 129.69,
          "en": "So all I wanna do in this action is I wanna reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.69,
          "end": 132.6,
          "en": "to my local storage and remove my token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.6,
          "end": 134.133,
          "en": "with the remove item method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.09,
          "end": 139.53,
          "en": "And then I want to return redirect with that redirect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.53,
          "end": 142.56,
          "en": "function from react-router-dom, and redirect the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.56,
          "end": 145.713,
          "en": "to the starting page; let's say if a user logs out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 148.11,
          "en": "So this might look strange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.11,
          "end": 151.983,
          "en": "but it is simply a JavaScript file, which holds an action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.06,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "And now I can register a new route that only has that action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 158.67000000000002,
          "en": "and no component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.67000000000002,
          "end": 160.89,
          "en": "And we learned about such routes before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.89,
          "end": 163.92000000000002,
          "en": "in the Routing section already, so that shouldn't be too",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.92000000000002,
          "end": 165.153,
          "en": "surprising or new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.07999999999998,
          "end": 170.603,
          "en": "I'll add a new route here where the path is simply logout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 176.22,
          "en": "and where the action is that log out action I just created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.22,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll import that action here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 184.28,
          "en": "and import action as logoutAction from ./pages/Logout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.79,
          "end": 190.95,
          "en": "And this logout action is now connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.95,
          "end": 192.423,
          "en": "to this newly added route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.47,
          "end": 196.02,
          "en": "Now we can send a request to this route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.02,
          "end": 200.25,
          "en": "We can submit a form that targets this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.25,
          "end": 203.15,
          "en": "and that's exactly what I'll do in my main navigation now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.3,
          "end": 206.25,
          "en": "I'll wrap my button here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.25,
          "end": 210.32999999999998,
          "en": "with this form that's provided by react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.32999999999998,
          "end": 215.32999999999998,
          "en": "So I import form here, and then I'll add an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.82,
          "end": 220.07999999999998,
          "en": "of /logout and a method of post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.07999999999998,
          "end": 222.753,
          "en": "though that doesn't matter here, and save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.71,
          "end": 226.17000000000002,
          "en": "With that, we have this log out button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.17000000000002,
          "end": 228.753,
          "en": "which we can click and we are redirected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.74,
          "end": 233.16,
          "en": "So that works as it should also got no errors here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 234.256,
          "en": "And if we take a look at our application tab here now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.256,
          "end": 239.163,
          "en": "we see that the token was removed from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.21,
          "end": 242.1,
          "en": "So that's how we can log out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.1,
          "end": 244.95,
          "en": "And now with that, we can finally also make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.95,
          "end": 248.04,
          "en": "that we update the UI accordingly and check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.04,
          "end": 250.59,
          "en": "whether we have a token or not to then, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.59,
          "end": 252.27,
          "en": "show the logout button only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.27,
          "end": 256.56,
          "en": "if we are logged in and show the authentication item here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.56,
          "end": 259.14300000000003,
          "en": "Only if we're not logged in, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}